<title>HONG KONG: China Merchants Hai Hong buys two tankers.</title>
<headline>China Merchants Hai Hong buys two tankers.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China Merchants Hai Hong Holdings Co Ltd said on Friday its 75 percent owned subsidiary Ming Wah Universal (Bermuda) Co Ltd has agreed to buy two crude oil carriers from Namura Shipbuilding Co Ltd and Sumitomo Corp.</p>
<p>The company did not disclose the value of deal but said a circular giving details of the transaction would be sent to shareholders on or before December 23.</p>
<p>It did not provide details of the two ships.</p>
<p>Hai Hong said the purchase had been approved by parent China Merchants Holdings (Hong Kong) Co Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
</text>
